Capability sentinel for the pro-down-workflow probe.

The probe executes committed fixtures under testdata/workflows/pro-down
through the real Ptah CLI. It proves the rollback contracts decided in
stokaro/ptah#810 and #971: `atlas migrate apply` records Atlas-format revision
rows on a real SQLite database, and both formatted and default-output
`atlas migrate down` runs — no stdin, Ptah-only `--confirm`, or
`--revision-format` flag — must read exactly those rows, execute the embedded
txtar down bodies, and clear the revision history. The formatted partial
rollback must also report the reverted migration and reach the matching live
database end state (before #810 the bare verb read Ptah's native revision
table and silently rolled back nothing; before #971 both paths prompted
interactively). Atlas keeps `migrate down` in its
proprietary Pro build, so these fixtures are intentionally separate from
the Atlas schema round-trip corpus (stokaro/ptah#758).
